A||||5||Doni Hagan||A/C Compressor question?||||1||
Z||000000||Doni Hagan||12-12-2001||10:03 PM||||Will the compressor from a 4-cyl fit a V-6? I know the mounts themselves should be different but is it the same basic unit? If so I have access to several in working condition and want to get a spare or two. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-12-2001||10:19 PM||||It depends on which 4 cyl we are talking about here.  I know that all V6's had Harrison A6 units, but the 87-88 fours had a Delphi DA-V5 variable displacement unit.  The mounts are not the same I do not think, and also, the DA-V5 units are spun by a serpent belt, where as the other ones (earlier four cylinders included) are spun by a V-belt.<P>Also, the electrical connections between the A6 and V5 may be different as well.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Doni Hagan||12-12-2001||10:51 PM||||What about the pre-87 fours? Might they use the same unit? The cars I'm looking at all all pre-87. <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/WAY2SLO_15.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||12-12-2001||10:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Doni Hagan:<BR><B>What about the pre-87 fours? Might they use the same unit? The cars I'm looking at all all pre-87. <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/WAY2SLO_15.jpg">   <P>[This message has been edited by Doni Hagan (edited 12-12-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>It is possible, since they are both driven by V-belts and have low and high pressure switches (I think).<P>The main reason that they added the DA-V5 unit to the 87-88 2.5's is becuase there wouldnt be a surge of power loss when the compressor engaged, all pressure control is controlled with valves and stuff inside the unit.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||12-13-2001||10:51 PM||||most of the A6 family units should be direct replacement as far as compressor. There may be small variations in the pulley offset to watch for but that's just an issue of changing a clutch. <P>GM put a whole bunch of new things in the 87's 4 cyl. DIS, 700 series TBI, and DA-V5 AC are the main ones. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Kasdan||12-14-2001||08:35 AM||||Im also having a slight a/c compressor issue...I removed all the bolts to the compressor (86 GT), and its stil snug in there, so its not bouncing around, but anyways, how can i get it out of there?  I cant pull it out the top (its amazing how much space my p/s compressor takes up) and the cat. converter is in the way of taking it out the bottom.  can i disconnect the exhaust before the cat and just drop the exhaust and pull the compressor out?  or is there an easier way?<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
